    "body": "@domenic the issue is discussed at length [here](https://github.com/WICG/web-share-target/issues/74#issuecomment-460519779) but basically the problem trying to be solved is that if developers only specify file extensions, but the platform only uses mime types (e.g. android), then their site won't work well on that platform. There are different ways of solving that, but one would be to force developers to specify a mapping such that each file extension corresponds to a mime type. There are other options listed in the bug linked above.\r\n\r\n@jakearchibald pointed out that the problem isn't specific to Web Share Target which is why we filed the bug here.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
